{
  "page": 7,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (05/2025)",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        27.39893913269043,
        368.4171447753906,
        37.36153793334961
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4.1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        84.90992736816406,
        86.00741577148438,
        93.75672149658203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For fixed rewards, D-MPC is comparable to other offline RL methods",
      "bbox": [
        96.96627807617188,
        84.90992736816406,
        413.4980773925781,
        93.75672149658203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We evaluate the performance of our proposed D-MPC on various D4RL (Fu et al., 2020) tasks. Planning-based",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        105.21894836425781,
        540.1913452148438,
        115.18154907226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approaches are especially beneficial in cases where we do not have access to expert data. As a result, we",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        117.17390441894531,
        540.2481689453125,
        127.13650512695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "focus our comparisons on cases where we learn with sub-optimal data. We experiment with locomotion tasks",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        129.12892150878906,
        540.1906127929688,
        139.09152221679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for Halfcheetah, Hopper and Walker2D for levels medium and medium-replay, Adroit tasks for pen, door and",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        141.0839385986328,
        540.2001953125,
        151.04653930664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hammer with cloned data, and Franka Kitchen tasks with mixed and partial data.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        153.0388946533203,
        431.6796875,
        163.00149536132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our results are summarized in Table 2. We see that our method significantly beats MBOP, and a behavior",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        170.97193908691406,
        540.4078369140625,
        180.93453979492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cloning (BC) baseline. It also marginally beats Diffuser, a strong model-based offline RL approach that uses",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        182.92689514160156,
        540.1854858398438,
        192.88949584960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "classifier guidance during sampling for planning instead of MPC. In contrast to Diffuser’s single diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        194.8819122314453,
        540.2277221679688,
        204.84451293945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model for joint state-action sequence generation, our approach decouples the dynamics model and action",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        206.83790588378906,
        540.227783203125,
        216.80050659179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proposal. We note that the total compute of our two transformers is designed to be roughly equivalent to",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        218.7929229736328,
        540.2022705078125,
        228.75552368164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diffuser’s single model; we achieve this by using a smaller transformer for the dynamics model, reflecting its",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        230.74794006347656,
        540.2249755859375,
        240.71054077148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "relative simplicity. We additionally compare to other popular model-free offline RL methods, like conservative",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        242.70289611816406,
        540.20166015625,
        252.66549682617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q-learning (CQL) (Kumar et al., 2020) and implicit Q-learning (IQL) (Kostrikov et al., 2021), as well as",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        254.6579132080078,
        540.13623046875,
        264.6205139160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model-based RL methods like MOReL (Kidambi et al., 2020), and sequence-models like Decision Transformer",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        266.6129150390625,
        540.3871459960938,
        276.5755310058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(DT) (Chen et al., 2021). These methods cannot adapt to novel rewards at test time (unlike D-MPC, MBOP",
      "bbox": [
        70.83399963378906,
        278.56890869140625,
        540.1585083007812,
        288.5315246582031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and Diffuser), but we include them to give a sense of the SOTA performance on this benchmark. We see",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        290.5238952636719,
        540.2177124023438,
        300.48651123046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that our method, despite its extra flexibility, can still match the performance of these existing, but more",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        302.4789123535156,
        540.2277221679688,
        312.4415283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "restrictive, methods.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        314.43389892578125,
        161.05564880371094,
        324.3965148925781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
